{{- /*
customers.gohtml is the customer list.

The rows come from the cross-module read layer, not from a module's service: the
panel knows no module (ADR 0011). Every field is printed as an ordinary value,
so the template engine's escaping applies to all of them — a customer's name is
text they supplied themselves and the panel runs inside an administrator's
session.

A shop's GUEST records outnumber its accounts, so the two are told apart in
their own column: it is the first thing an operator looks for on this screen.
*/ -}}
{{ define "body" }}
<h1>{{ .Title }}</h1>

{{ if .Customers }}
<div class="scroll">
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Name</th><th>Email</th><th>Account</th><th>Since</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {{ range .Customers }}
    <tr>
      <td>
        <a href="{{ $.Path }}/{{ .ID }}">
          {{ if .Name }}{{ .Name }}{{ else }}<span class="muted">no name</span>{{ end }}
        </a>
      </td>
      <td>{{ if .Email }}{{ .Email }}{{ else }}<span class="muted">no address</span>{{ end }}</td>
      <td>
        {{ if .HasAccount }}
          <span class="pill">registered</span>
        {{ else }}
          <span class="pill">guest</span>
        {{ end }}
      </td>
      <td>{{ if not .CreatedAt.IsZero }}{{ .CreatedAt.Format "2006-01-02" }}{{ end }}</td>
    </tr>
  {{ end }}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
{{ else }}
<p class="muted">No customers on this page.</p>
{{ end }}

<nav>
  {{ if .HasPrev }}<a href="{{ .Path }}?page={{ .PrevPage }}">Previous</a>{{ end }}
  <span class="muted">Page {{ .Page }}</span>
  {{ if .HasNext }}<a href="{{ .Path }}?page={{ .NextPage }}">Next</a>{{ end }}
</nav>
{{ end }}
